This area, known as the Onandaga Park and Strathmore Sections, is located in the south-western part of the city. The terrain is level to rolling and hilly. It is nicely wooded section with lots ranging from 45’ to 75’ in width; 95% developed; homes are of the bungalow (square or mixed pattern) type; all utilities are installed. The area, generally, has a pleasing appearance. The Strathmore Section (south end of area) is restricted to single residences. Homes facing Onandaga Park are more substantial in character and range up to $15,000 in value; the newer section adjoins Bellevue Country Club; the section between Claremont and Summit measures up nicely but that lying between Stolp to Crossott is of a slightly poorer grade than rest of the area. The area, on the whole, is holding up fairly well and is rated a good first grade. Typical Sales: |Address| Type of Property| Sales Price and Terms| Remarks| (
